From 06d96723d0a5aaf8a36daa4576670e347d94e4f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:02:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] fix: use the CGI connection address in service URLs

Address selection from a configured interface or a route to the client
can advertise a different local endpoint on a multihomed device. Prefer
the web server CGI SERVER_ADDR value and share address resolution between
text and JSON configuration readers.

Fixes: cdc5939bbe97 ("feat: auto-detect local address from REMOTE_ADDR; ifs= now optional override")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 conf.c            | 114 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------
 test/test_cgi.py  |  23 +++++++++-
 test/test_http.py |  17 +++++--
 3 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 69 deletions(-)

--- a/conf.c
+++ b/conf.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
